        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patrick White; Katherine Anne Porter\n- Works: The Tree of Man; Noon Wine\n- Roles: writer; novelist; journalist; essayist; short story writer; political activist\n- Awards: Nobel Prize in Literature\n\nFacts:\n- Katherine Anne Porter was born on May 15, 1890, and died on September 18, 1980.\n- Patrick White was born on May 28, 1912, and died on September 30, 1990.\n- Katherine Anne Porter was an American journalist, essayist, short story writer, novelist, and political activist.\n- Patrick White was an Australian writer who is widely regarded as one of the most important English-language novelists of the 20th century.\n- Noon Wine is a 1937 short novel by American author Katherine Anne Porter.\n- Patrick White won the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1973.\n- The Tree of Man is the fourth published novel by Australian novelist Patrick White.",
